# V-P-13 carries `ASSESSMENT_DIGEST`, which is `[0x33; 32]` (H-04). Unlike the entries above, this
# file was written after the 24 September deployment published that constant, so it does not predate
# it — but the direction of travel is the same and is the only thing that matters: `0x3333…3333` is
# this repository's generator constant, used by every record vector, and the harness sent it to a
# throwaway program. Nothing about V-P-13 borrows from that deployment.
#
# Every future vector carrying a record will need a line like this one. That is the standing cost of
# listing the two repository-authored placeholders rather than narrowing the rule to exclude them,
# which was the owner's call to make and was not taken. H-45 (#137) records the choice.
vectors/V-P-13.json  0x3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333  the generator's own ASSESSMENT_DIGEST, which a devnet harness happened to publish to a superseded program
